{
  "id": "fluency-l6-working-backwards",
  "lesson": "l6-working-backwards",
  "title": "Fluency: antiderivatives of powers",
  "n": 20,
  "pass": 0.9,
  "minutes": 10,
  "families": [
    {
      "id": "power",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "integrate a power",
      "vars": {
        "k": { "int": [2, 7] },
        "a": { "int": [-12, 12], "not": [0] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "t"] }
      },
      "let": { "k1": "k + 1", "r": "a/(k + 1)" },
      "where": ["r != 1 and r != -1"],
      "prompt": "Find $\\int {a:c}{v}^{{{k}}}\\,d{v}$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{r:frac}{v}^{{{k1}}}", "upToConstant": true, "keyboard": "calculus" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "old-power", "tex": "{a/k:frac}{v}^{{{k1}}}", "line": "You divided by {k}, the old power. Divide by the new power, {k1}." },
        { "id": "no-divide", "tex": "{a:c}{v}^{{{k1}}}", "line": "You raised the power to {k1} but did not divide by {k1}." },
        { "id": "differentiated", "tex": "{a*k}{v}^{{{k - 1}}}", "line": "You differentiated. We want the function whose derivative is ${a:c}{v}^{{{k}}}$." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Raise the power by one, to {k1}, then divide the coefficient ${a}$ by {k1}.",
        "So $\\int {a:c}{v}^{{{k}}}\\,d{v} = {r:frac}{v}^{{{k1}}} + C$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "polynomial",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "integrate a polynomial term by term",
      "vars": {
        "p": { "int": [-3, 3], "not": [0] },
        "q": { "int": [-4, 4], "not": [0] },
        "c": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [-1, 0, 1] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "t"] }
      },
      "let": { "a": "3*p", "b": "2*q" },
      "prompt": "Find $\\int ({poly(v; a, b, c)})\\,d{v}$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{poly(v; p, q, c, 0)}", "upToConstant": true, "keyboard": "calculus" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "no-divide", "tex": "{poly(v; a, b, c, 0)}", "line": "You raised each power by one but did not divide by the new power." },
        { "id": "constant-left", "tex": "{poly(v; p, q, 0, 0)}{c:+}", "line": "The constant {c} integrates to ${c}{v}$, not {c}." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Integrate term by term: ${a} \\div 3 = {p}$ and ${b} \\div 2 = {q}$.",
        "The constant ${c}$ integrates to ${c}{v}$.",
        "So the answer is ${poly(v; p, q, c, 0)} + C$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "negative-power",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "integrate a negative power",
      "vars": {
        "k": { "int": [2, 6] },
        "m": { "int": [-6, 6], "not": [0] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "t"] }
      },
      "let": { "k1": "k - 1", "c": "m*(k - 1)", "e": "1 - k" },
      "where": ["c != 1 and c != -1"],
      "prompt": "Find $\\int {c}{v}^{{-{k}}}\\,d{v}$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{-m:c}{v}^{{{e}}}", "upToConstant": true, "keyboard": "calculus" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "power-lowered", "tex": "{-c/(k + 1):frac}{v}^{{{-k - 1}}}", "line": "You lowered the power to {-k - 1}. Raise it by one, to {e}." },
        { "id": "sign-lost", "tex": "{m:c}{v}^{{{e}}}", "line": "The new power is {e}, so you divide by {e}, which flips the sign." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Raise the power by one: ${-k} + 1 = {e}$. Then divide by {e}.",
        "${c} \\div ({e}) = {-m}$, so $\\int {c}{v}^{{-{k}}}\\,d{v} = {-m:c}{v}^{{{e}}} + C$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fix-constant",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "fix the constant from a value",
      "vars": {
        "k": { "int": [2, 3] },
        "m": { "int": [-3, 3], "not": [0] },
        "p": { "int": [-2, 2] },
        "q0": { "int": [-9, 9] },
        "r": { "int": [-2, 2] }
      },
      "let": { "k1": "k + 1", "c": "m*(k + 1)", "fp": "m*p^(k + 1)", "fr": "m*r^(k + 1)", "cc": "q0 - m*p^(k + 1)", "ans": "m*r^(k + 1) + q0 - m*p^(k + 1)" },
      "where": ["r != p", "r^k1 != p^k1", "cc != 0", "fr != q0 + c*(r^k1 - p^k1)"],
      "prompt": "A function has $F'(x) = {c}x^{{{k}}}$ and $F({p}) = {q0}$. Work out $F({r})$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{ans}", "tol": { "abs": 0 } },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "no-constant", "value": "{fr}", "line": "You left out the constant. Use $F({p}) = {q0}$ to find it first." },
        { "id": "no-divide", "value": "{q0 + c*(r^k1 - p^k1)}", "line": "You raised the power to {k1} but did not divide by {k1}." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "$F(x) = {m:c}x^{{{k1}}} + C$.",
        "$F({p}) = {fp} + C = {q0}$, so $C = {cc}$.",
        "$F({r}) = {fr}{cc:+} = {ans}$."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
